    {
      "id": "key-text",
      "shape": "text",
      "role": "label",
      "face": "body",
      "text": "Refinement of chapter 3’s final-outcome step for start-session.\nBlue: steps in deciding the outcome. Grey: outcomes.\nApplicable cleanup is attempted before reporting an outcome.\nThis order expresses precedence, not the implementation’s call order.\nOriginal failures keep their status when later cleanup also fails.\nCancellation suppresses a published result and retains other diagnostics.\nGreen: the only success route. Empty publication is a valid value.\nA later nonzero child exit does not invalidate that value.\nA failed final write can leave a prefix; a late signal can interrupt it.\nend-session, help and version invocations are covered by the table, not this view.",
      "x": 368.8037109375,
      "y": 800.87734375,
      "anchor": "center",
      "align": "center",
      "wrapped": false,
      "w": 571.662109375,
      "h": 175.6671875
    }
